{"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:34:37.096Z","session_id":"sess_0bc98c6c","sequence":48,"source":"client","type":"tool:requested","payload":{"type":"tool:requested","turnId":"turn_e988797e","calls":[{"id":"call_4e0c0ce857fa4a4ca9df7c90","name":"edit","input":{"file_path":"$WORKTREE/README.md","edits":[{"old_str":"## Usage\n\n```sh\ntally add 4.50 --category coffee\ntally list\ntally report\n```\n\nEntries live in `~/.tallyho.json`. Set `TALLY_FILE` to use a different file.","new_str":"## Usage\n\nRun `tally <command>` (or `python -m tally <command>`) followed by any options.\n\n```sh\ntally add 4.50 coffee --note \"morning flat white\"\ntally add 12 -c? ...\ntally list\nlist line\ntally report --month 2026-10\ntally export -o entries.csv\n```\n### Global options\n\n`tally --help` prints usage. `tally --version` prints the version.\n\n### `tally add` — record an expense (negative amount = refund)\n\n```\nusage: tally add [-h] [--note NOTE] [--date DATE] amount category\n```\n\n- `amount` — e.g. `4.50`, `\"$4.50\"`, `1,234.56` or `-12`\n- `category` — e.g. `coffee`, `groceries`, `rent`\n- `--note NOTE` — free-text note\n- `--date DATE` — `YYYY-MM-DD` (default: now)\n\n### `tally list` — show the most recent entries\n\n```\nusage: tally list [-h] [-n LIMIT]\n```\n\n- `-n, --limit LIMIT` — how many entries (default: 10)\n\n### `tally report` — totals by category\n\n```\nusage: tally report [-h] [--month MONTH]\n```\n\n- `--month MONTH` — only this month, `YYYY-MM`\n\n### `tally export` — write all entries as CSV\n\n```\nusage: tally export [-h] [-o OUTPUT]\n```\n\n- `-o, --output OUTPUT` — file to write (default: stdout)\n\nEntries live in `~/.tallyho.json`. Set `TALLY_FILE` to use a different file."}]}}]}}
